# Cloudflare Pages redirects — DocScan Pro Web
# ===============================================
# Cloudflare Pages evaluates _redirects top-to-bottom and the FIRST
# matching rule wins. The prebuilt Expo web export emits real .html
# files for every known route (dashboard.html, scan.html, etc.) AND
# static assets under /assets/, /_expo/, /static/, /icons/. Cloudflare
# Pages will serve those files automatically — but ONLY when no
# redirect rule claims the URL. A catch-all `/* /index.html 200`
# claims every URL, including /assets/* and /icons/*, and rewrites
# them to index.html with Content-Type: text/html. That's the bug
# that was breaking every icon font on the live site.
#
# Strategy:
#   1) Pass-through rewrites for every static-asset directory, using
#      splat capture so the rewritten URL still hits the static file.
#   2) A literal pass-through for each prerendered HTML route so the
#      catch-all below doesn't intercept /dashboard, /scan, etc.
#   3) The catch-all `/*` goes LAST, only matching truly-unknown paths.
#
# Per Cloudflare, rules with no splats/placeholders perform better
# when placed above splat-bearing rules — ordering is cosmetic but
# removes a parser warning.

# ============================================================
# Static asset passthroughs (must come before the catch-all)
# ============================================================

# --- Literal asset paths at the site root (no splats, fast path) ---
/favicon.ico                    /favicon.ico                    200
/favicon-16x16.png              /favicon-16x16.png              200
/favicon-32x32.png              /favicon-32x32.png              200
/apple-touch-icon.png           /apple-touch-icon.png           200
/manifest.json                  /manifest.json                  200
/robots.txt                     /robots.txt                     200
/BingSiteAuth.xml               /BingSiteAuth.xml               200
/og-image.png                   /og-image.png                   200
/twitter-image.png              /twitter-image.png              200
/google-site-verification.html  /google-site-verification.html  200
/yandex_30228b25e87e4a62.html   /yandex_30228b25e87e4a62.html   200
/sitemap.xml                    /sitemap.xml                    200
/sitemap-images.xml             /sitemap-images.xml             200
/_sitemap.html                  /_sitemap.html                  200
/+not-found.html                /+not-found.html                200

# --- Splat-bearing asset directories (intercepts asset URLs) ---
# Rewrite to self via :splat so the static file gets served. The first
# match wins, blocking the catch-all below from firing on these paths.
#
# /assets/node_modules/* — Cloudflare Pages is reached via wrangler
# `pages deploy`, which has a hardcoded IGNORE_LIST that skips files
# under /node_modules/ paths (cloudflare/workers-sdk#3615, won't fix).
# Expo Metro emits Expo vector-icons fonts + react-navigation icons
# under /assets/node_modules/... — the very files wrangler skips. The
# CI workflow renames that dir to /assets/_nm/ before deploy, so this
# rule translates the JS bundle's hardcoded /assets/node_modules/*
# references to the real on-disk path /assets/_nm/:splat.
/assets/node_modules/*  /assets/_nm/:splat  200
/assets/*              /assets/:splat      200
/_expo/*               /_expo/:splat       200
/static/*              /static/:splat      200
/icons/*               /icons/:splat       200
/blog/*                /blog/:splat        200
/document/*            /document/:splat    200
/(tabs)/*              /(tabs)/:splat      200

# ============================================================
# SPA catch-all — must be LAST
# ============================================================
# Any path not already claimed (true client-side routes) gets the SPA
# shell so Expo Router can take over.
/*    /index.html    200
